                "text": "To solve  \n\\[\n\\sin(x) + x^2 = 42,\n\\]\nrewrite as finding roots of\n\\[\nf(x)=\\sin(x)+x^2-42.\n\\]\n\nSince \\(x^2\\) dominates, solutions should be near \\(\\pm\\sqrt{42}\\approx \\pm 6.4807\\). Using numerical root-finding gives two real solutions:\n\n\\[\nx \\approx 6.4666500409\n\\]\n\\[\nx \\approx -6.4970982170\n\\]\n\nSo the equation has **two real solutions**, approximately:\n\\[\n\\boxed{x \\approx 6.46665 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x \\approx -6.49710.}\n\\]",
